{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_repo_size_size_audit", "label": "The repository size audit", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/REPO-SIZE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Measured 2026-09-02 at 8 commits with find, du and git count-objects; historical, and superseded by any figure docfigures.py pins."}, {"id": "docs_repo_size_pack_versus_checkout", "label": "The clone is 83 MiB, not 508 MiB", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/REPO-SIZE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "225 Markdown files are successive builds of one lineage and git delta-compresses each against its neighbours, so clone and push cost is governed by the pack and not by the checkout."}, {"id": "docs_repo_size_duplicate_blobs", "label": "Deleting duplicates is a poor size lever", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/REPO-SIZE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "416 tracked paths resolve to 297 unique blobs; the duplicate paths cost checkout size and essentially nothing in the pack, because identical content is already stored once."}, {"id": "docs_repo_size_github_limits", "label": "GitHub's published limits", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/REPO-SIZE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "50 MiB warning, 100 MiB hard block applying to the blob anywhere in history, 2 GB per push, ~5 GB repository soft limit."}, {"id": "docs_repo_size_trigger_points", "label": "Five trigger points, and LFS is the last remedy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/REPO-SIZE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The real trigger for LFS is a 1 GiB pack, b